# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and in every working
# tree, regardless of the cloner's core.autocrlf setting.
#
# This is not cosmetic. Tincture.Font.Standard parses the base-14 metric
# tables out of priv/standard_fonts/eg_font_*.erl with regexes anchored as
# `;$` under /m, and Erlang's :re treats LF alone as the newline. A CRLF
# checkout leaves a \r before every \n, no width line matches, and the
# registry silently loads zero glyph widths — so every string measures 0.0
# wide and the typography, line-breaking and PDF fixture suites fail with
# arithmetic assertions that point nowhere near the real cause.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads: never eligible for newline conversion or textual diff.
# The PDF fixtures are byte-locked against checked-in SHA-256 digests, so a
# single substituted byte breaks test/tincture/pdf_fixture_lock_test.exs.
*.pdf binary
*.cub binary
